## Home navigation: launch tiles with illustrations and live counts

Context: On Home, the Browse / Bridges / My tasks tab rail is replaced by three
large launch tiles (Contexts, Bridges, My tasks). Each tile has an inline SVG
illustration and a live count. The selected panel renders below the tiles.
Only the Home page changes; other pages keep their tab rails.

Changes:
1. src/front/templates/home.html: tab rail replaced by `.home-nav-tiles`
   (`#homeTabs`, three `.home-nav-tile` buttons with inline SVG art, count
   spans `#homeCountContexts` / `#homeCountBridges` / `#homeCountTasks`, title
   and description). Panel card no longer uses `ob-tabs-wrap`.
2. src/front/static/home/css/home.css: launch tile styles (grid, hover, active,
   focus-visible, count, art sizing, responsive stacking below 768px).
3. src/front/static/home/js/home.js: loads the Contexts count from
   `/domain/list-projects` on init.
4. src/front/static/home/js/home-tasks.js: sets the My tasks count from the
   same `/review/my-tasks` response it already renders; `—` on error.
5. src/front/static/registry/js/registry.js: sets the Bridges count when bridge
   data loads (lazy: `—` until the Bridges tile/tab is first opened).
6. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-18-home-registry-design.md: navigation section
   revised to launch tiles.
7. docs/development.md: Home page contract row updated.
8. tests/units/front/test_clarity_design_contract.py,
   tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py,
   tests/units/front/test_registry_operational_status.py: assertions moved from
   the tab rail to the launch tiles.

