## Home launch tiles open an 80% Registry modal

Context: The Contexts / Bridges / My tasks content no longer renders under the
launch tiles. Clicking a tile opens an 80% viewport modal with that section.
A compact switcher in the modal header lets you move between sections without
closing. Deep links ``?section=…`` auto-open the modal.

Changes:
1. src/front/templates/home.html: panel card removed; content moved into
   ``#homeRegistryModal`` (80% dialog). Header carries title, section switcher
   (Contexts / Bridges / My tasks), ``#registryStatus``, and close.
2. src/front/static/home/js/home.js: tile click → open modal + activate
   section; header switcher uses Bootstrap tabs; ``?section=`` opens modal;
   closing clears the URL section; Bridges re-dispatched on ``shown.bs.modal``
   for graph layout.
3. src/front/static/home/css/home.css: 80vw/80vh modal layout; Bridges flex
   fill restored for the modal body; launch tiles unchanged.
4. tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py,
   tests/units/front/test_clarity_design_contract.py,
   tests/units/front/test_registry_modal_loading.py,
   tests/e2e/registry/test_registry_flows.py: assert modal + tiles contract.

